\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The $(\text  {field}\times \text  {momentum})$ plane. Region coverage is about $90\%$, closed by the theorems G2.1--G2.4. The one open cell --- typical field with high momentum --- is the region where all four handles fail simultaneously: the WSTC exponent vanishes when the field is typical, the AF--UV suppression has not begun at $g\approx 1.5$, and the $N/12$ floor is roughly ten times too small. That cell is exactly $\operatorname  {Var}(\xi _{k\to 0})\le 1/\lambda $, with zero slack.}}{22}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
