\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces The Banks--Zaks conformal window for $\mathrm  {SU}(3)$ with $N_f$ massless fundamentals. The window is real: those theories are asymptotically free, single-coupling, and gapless in the infrared. Pure Yang--Mills sits at $N_f=0$, a distance of nine to twelve units of $N_f$ below the perturbative boundary, while the loop-by-loop shift of that boundary is about $+3$. Hence the question is not marginal --- but ``$N_f=0$ is outside the window'' is rigorous only perturbatively; its nonperturbative form is exactly $(G1)$.}}{51}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:window}{{12}{51}{The Banks--Zaks conformal window for $\mathrm {SU}(3)$ with $N_f$ massless fundamentals. The window is real: those theories are asymptotically free, single-coupling, and gapless in the infrared. Pure Yang--Mills sits at $N_f=0$, a distance of nine to twelve units of $N_f$ below the perturbative boundary, while the loop-by-loop shift of that boundary is about $+3$. Hence the question is not marginal --- but ``$N_f=0$ is outside the window'' is rigorous only perturbatively; its nonperturbative form is exactly $(G1)$}{figure.caption.22}{}}
